opens-after.l4:13:1-17:
  `opens on day 2` can start itself again: a HENCE or LEST in it leads back to `opens on day 2`.
  I could not check that this comes to an end, because one of its duties opens at a time counted from a fixed moment (AFTER … OF …), so its deadline is fixed too, and once that is past, each new copy is already late.
  
  If it does come to an end, say why on a line of its own above `opens on day 2`, like this:
  
    @ends-because <your reason>
  
  A reader can then check your reason, and L4 stops warning about it.
